ce Bottoms ahead by roughly one to three points, though the most recent survey, from a Republican-leaning pollster in mid-September, gave Jackson a three-point edge. Local coverage describes a dead heat heading into the fall debates.\n\nPrediction markets put Bottoms's chances near 58-59%, and rating outlets split between Tossup and a Democratic lean. The fundamentals cut both ways: Georgia leans slightly Republican, but the 2026 environment favors Democrats, and Jackson has raised vastly more money — about $119 million to Bottoms's $5.8 million — leaving him a large cash advantage for the closing stretch. The forecast expects a narrow Democratic margin with wide uncertainty, firmly in tossup territory.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6414, "margin": 1.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.628, "margin": 1.5}]}